<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 9 September, from 9 to 1956.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">9 CE <span class="tih-ago">2,017 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germanic tribes destroy three Roman legions in the Teutoburg Forest</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arminius">Arminius</a> led Germanic warriors in an ambush that wiped out three legions under Varus over several days, by tradition ending around this date. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> never again tried to conquer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arminius">Arminius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1000">1000 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,026 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Olaf Tryggvason falls at the Battle of Svolder</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a large naval battle in the western Baltic, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-tryggvason">Olaf Tryggvason</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> was defeated and killed by an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweyn-forkbeard">Sweyn Forkbeard</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olof-skotkonung">Olof Skötkonung</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and Eric Haakonsson, Earl of Lade. The victors divided Norway between them.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-svolder">Battle of Svolder</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1087">1087 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">939 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William the Conqueror dies in Rouen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">William I died of injuries received at the burning of Mantes. Normandy went to his eldest son Robert and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-england">William Rufus</a>, a division that set his heirs against each other.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1141">1141 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">885 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Yelü Dashi's Qara Khitai rout the Seljuks at Qatwan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the Qatwan steppe north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yelu-dashi">Yelü Dashi</a> encircled and destroyed the army of the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-sanjar">Ahmad Sanjar</a>, who barely escaped. The defeat cost the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> all of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> and ended their authority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qatwan">Battle of Qatwan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yelu-dashi">Yelü Dashi</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1493">1493 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">533 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ottoman raiders defeat a Croatian army at Krbava Field</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the Krbava plain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lika">Lika</a>, Ottoman raiders under Hadım Yakub Pasha heavily defeated a Croatian army under Ban Emerik Derenčin. The ban was captured and many nobles were killed, opening <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> to further Ottoman raids.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-krbava-field">Battle of Krbava Field</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress adopts the name 'United States of America'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-congress">Continental Congress</a> resolved that wherever 'United Colonies' had been used, the new nation should be styled the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>'. The name had appeared in the Declaration two months earlier.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1850">1850 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">176 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">California becomes the 31st US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> entered the Union as a free state under the Compromise of 1850, two years after gold was found at Sutter's Mill. Its admission upset the balance between free and slave states.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1948">1948 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">North Korea is proclaimed under Kim Il-sung</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">Democratic People's Republic of Korea</a> was proclaimed in the Soviet-occupied north, weeks after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">Republic of Korea</a> in the south. Kim Il-sung founded a dynasty that still rules.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1956">1956 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">70 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elvis Presley first appears on The Ed Sullivan Show</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 60 million Americans, over 80 per cent of the TV audience, watched Elvis's first appearance on Sullivan's show. The 'waist up' camera shots came only on his third appearance in 1957.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 9 September <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cardinal-richelieu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cardinal-richelieu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Cardinal Richelieu</span><span class="tp">1585–1642</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/thomas-hutchinson-governor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thomas-hutchinson-governor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Thomas Hutchinson (governor)</span><span class="tp">1711–1780</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-bligh"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-bligh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Bligh</span><span class="tp">1754–1817</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sergio-osmena"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sergio-osmena.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sergio Osmeña</span><span class="tp">1878–1961</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
